= Secret Commonwealth Army Meeting

Through our intelligence work, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> has received a copy of minutes of a meeting between <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> leaders Gregor Crowde, Ulric Gorrick, and [? if not rohm_explode: Ernst Röhm?][? if rohm_explode: the leader of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span>?], with former General Edwin von Stülpnagel, a close ally of Staal.

The topic of the conference was about possible joint action between the Commonwealth Army and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span>, if the leftists were to make a move following the elections.

- @schleicher

@schleicher
title: Concerning.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_r -= 1; staal_marcher_support -= 1; royalist_urgency += 1; 

This all but confirms our suspicions that General Staal is conspiring with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> against the <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> forces. Our relations with the "Red General" has worsened.

- @schleicher_2

@schleicher_2
title: Von Staal offers to meet with the unions, and to ease their fears.
subtitle: The unions are independent of the party, and have agreed to participate.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_r += 1; staal_marcher_support += 1; labor_dissent += 5

The invitation for a direct meeting between Tobias Leighart, leader of the ADGB, and von Staal is declined. Instead, a larger meeting is held, including Goodryke, his Interior Minister, and the ADGB’s co-chairs.

At the meeting, the union leaders confront Staal over alleged secret agreements with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span>, prompting both Staal and Goodryke to strike a more conciliatory tone in response to union complaints about unfair government treatment. Staal denies any such deals with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span>, insisting that the government's highest priority is reducing unemployment. Goodryke also requests the unions to use their influence to persuade the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> to give the government time to deliver results.

By the end of the meeting, the three unionists are left impressed by Staal, who hints at possible concessions to a “patriotic labor movement.” A line of communication between the ADGB and the government remains open—much to Vesh’s frustration, as he aims to maintain a united front against the regime.

(Leighart is granted an ability)